{"author":"schacon@gmail.com","body":"## Summary\n\nAdd a \"writeups\" feature — a way to capture rough notes, ideas, and things to work on that aren't yet ready to be formal tickets. Think of them as pre-tickets or design notes that can evolve into one or more tickets over time.\n\n## Data Model\n\nEach writeup gets:\n- **UUID** — unique identifier, same as tickets (prefix-addressable)\n- **Title** — short summary\n- **Author** — who created it\n- **Versions** — ordered list of content revisions, each with:\n  - version UUID\n  - author (who wrote this version)\n  - timestamp\n  - content (markdown body)\n\nThe version list is key for multi-user collaboration — anyone can append a new version with updated thinking, and you get a full history of how the idea evolved. No conflicts, just append.\n\n## Storage\n\nStore under a parallel ref (e.g. `refs/meta/writeups`) or as a sub-namespace under the existing meta ref. Each writeup is a directory with:\n- `meta` file (title, author, created, tags)\n- `versions/` directory with one file per version (timestamp-sorted)\n\n## Multi-user Flow\n\n1. Alice creates a writeup: `ti writeup new --title \"rethink sync protocol\"`\n2. Alice adds content: `ti writeup edit <id>` (opens editor, saves as version 1)\n3. Bob syncs, reads it: `ti writeup show <id>`\n4. Bob adds thoughts: `ti writeup edit <id>` (appends version 2, authored by Bob)\n5. When ready, promote to ticket(s): `ti writeup promote <id>` (creates ticket from latest version, links back)\n\n## Commands\n\n- `ti writeup new --title \"...\"` — create a new writeup\n- `ti writeup list` — list all writeups\n- `ti writeup show <id>` — show writeup with version history\n- `ti writeup edit <id>` — append a new version\n- `ti writeup promote <id>` — convert to a ticket (or extract tickets from it)\n- `ti writeup archive <id>` — soft-archive without deleting\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should writeups support tags/labels for organization?\n- Should `promote` create a single ticket or allow splitting into multiple?\n- Should there be a way to link writeups to existing tickets (context/background)?\n- Inline comments on specific versions, or keep it simple with whole-version appends?"}